	(text "Hardware off timer: holding the power button for ~4-9 s turns the MCU rail off even if the firmware hangs\n(Q29 releases C172, U23 trips, Q30 pulls PWR-LATCH low). Firmware turns off at 3 s.\nWhile charging, the rail-hold (Q31 on BATTERY-CHARGER, from DC_IN) keeps the MCU rail on regardless,\nand charger power alone turns the MCU rail on (Q31 pulls PWR-SW-G low)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 434.34 389.89 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "05372955-2756-40df-8455-1a35676292a0")
	)
	(text "POWER MANAGMENT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.048 3.048)
				(thickness 0.6096)
				(bold yes)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0ab010c9-f43f-4c47-b617-b98b7f7f82d4")
	)
	(text "VM-VBAT (motors, fan) is on only while WD_OK is high (RC watchdog fed) AND ~{VM-VBAT-EN} is low.\nQ19 source-switched AND: GPIO low = on. R184 keeps it off in reset/flash. AO4407C: Vgs +/-25 V, no gate divider needed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 283.21 182.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "19fe543d-1f4a-4b45-a811-1a53dc4c513a")
	)
	(text "PCB mounting standoffs (Wurth WA-SMSI, M3), moved here from the removed M.2 sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 35.56 175.26 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "58743119-c61d-4faa-9f44-a8a3552e43c7")
	)
	(text "Old VM-5V switch removed: the LiDAR (VM-5V-LIDAR) and the water pump (VM-5V-WATER-PUMP)\nnow have their own WD_OK-gated switches on their sheets.\nNo soft ramp."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 383.54 110.49 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c60952ba-300f-42b7-8bc9-3b41711b6f9d")
	)
	(text "VUS = 0.6 V x (1 + 232k/10k) ~ 14.5 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 465.836 227.838 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "d8121408-7b4f-4c1a-92af-c064e178e8a5")
	)
	(text "Q1 (AO4407C) on VM-VBAT: ~5 A normal load is ~0.3-0.4 W; short stall peaks (~13 A) are fine with copper under the drain."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 398.78 83.82 0)
		(effects
